    "syllabusEnglish": "Mobile Programming",
    "credits": "3",
    "degreeLevel": "Bachelor",
    "timeAllocation": "Study hour (150h) = 45h contact hours + 1h final exam + 104h self-study",
    "prerequisite": "PRO192",
    "description": "1. Understand the fundamental concepts of mobile programming with Flutter and Dart.\n\n2. Experience using popular widgets and plugins to build cross-platform user interfaces.\n\n3. Knowledge of state management, form handling, and navigation between screens in mobile applications.\n\n4. Learn and apply asynchronous programming techniques with Future and async/await.\n\n5. Ability to integrate RESTful APIs to exchange data between mobile applications and servers, as well as store data locally using SharedPreferences and SQLite.\n\n6. Proficient in using Dart libraries and command-line tools to optimize the application development process.\n\n7. Knowledge of implementing mobile notification systems, including local and push notifications.",
    "studentTasks": "- Students must attend more than 80% of contact sessions in order to be accepted to the final examination.\n\n- Student is responsible to do all assigned exercises given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time\n\n- Use laptop in class only for learning purpose\n\n- Promptly access to the FU LMS at http://lms.fpt.edu.vn for up-to-date course information",
    "scoringScale": "10",
    "decisionNo": "1402/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 12/12/2025",
    "isApproved": 1,
    "note": "- Visual Studio Code (recommended, lightweight and supports many Flutter/Dart extensions).\n\n- Xcode (only needed if building & testing iOS, required on macOS).",
